# What this repository publishes: the module itself, how to build it, and the
# script that does the building. Everything else stays on the machine that made
# it — the notes this was tested with, the extracts taken from the Notes app, the
# hand-over notes that describe this device, and the signing key.
#
# The first block is a whitelist on purpose: a new file anywhere else is ignored
# unless somebody deliberately publishes it, so a stray export or a dump cannot
# be committed by accident.

/*
!/src/
!/res/
!/stubs/
!/assets/
!/AndroidManifest.xml
!/build.ps1
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/.gitignore

# The investigation's scripts are worth publishing (they are how the app's own
# capture path was worked out), but not the extracts they produce from the Notes
# app: those are somebody else's bytecode, and the scripts regenerate them from
# your own copy of the app.
!/build/
build/*
!build/*.py
!build/*.sh
!build/classlist.txt
!build/sources.txt
build/capture-classes.txt
build/capture-flow.txt
build/capture-helper.txt
build/capture-runnable.txt
build/capture-sites.txt
build/d1_capture_ctx.txt
build/editor-activity.txt
build/pipeline-classes.txt
build/screen-shot-utils.txt
build/watermark-targets.txt
# Scratch files the tools write as they run.
build/last-backup-dir.txt
build/last-export-stamp.txt
build/tmp-nearme_note.db

# Hand-over and build notes: they name this device, its ROM, the backup
# directories and a few note titles, so they are local documents, not releases.
/HANDOFF.md
/BUILD.md
/BACKUP.md

# Downloaded toolchain and extracted SDK used by build.ps1.
/.buildtools/

# The signing key is private to this machine; build.ps1 regenerates it.
/keystore/

# Scratch directories created by the tools while working on a device dump.
/notesdb-*/
/.verify-*/

# Generated test output.
/test/out/
